BBIIOOSS3322
     At system startup, the BIOS is scanned for the BIOS32 Service Directory
     (part of the PCI specification), and the existence of the directory is
     recorded.  This can then be used to locate other services.

     bbiiooss3322__SSDDllooookkuupp()     Attempts to locate the BIOS32 service matching the
                           4-byte identifier passed in the _i_d_e_n_t field of the
                           _e_n_t argument.

     bbiiooss3322()              Calls a bios32 function.  This presumes that the
                           function is capable of working within the kernel
                           segment (normally the case).  The virtual address
                           of the entrypoint is supplied in _e_n_t_r_y and the reg‐
                           ister arguments to the function are supplied in
                           _a_r_g_s.

     PCIbios               If not NULL, points to a _s_t_r_u_c_t _b_i_o_s_3_2___S_D_e_n_t_r_y
                           structure describing the PCI BIOS entrypoint which
